What:		/sys/kernel/wakelock_profiler/ap_resume_reason_stastics
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only OnePlus standby-resume attribution counters. Each line
		contains a wake-source category name followed by its count. The
		vendor spelling of "stastics" is part of the userspace ABI.

What:		/sys/kernel/wakelock_profiler/wakeup_stastisc_reset
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write reset control for the resume attribution counters. Reads
		return "reset". Write the string "reset" to clear the counters.
		The vendor spelling of "stastisc" is part of the userspace ABI.

What:		/sys/kernel/wakelock_profiler/modem_resume_reason_stastics
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only leading modem wake reason. The result is exported in the
		vendor NAME:COUNT:TOTAL format. The vendor spelling of
		"stastics" is part of the userspace ABI.

What:		/sys/kernel/wakelock_profiler/kernel_time
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only accumulated kernel wakelock time in milliseconds. Writing
		"reset" starts a new accumulation interval.

What:		/sys/kernel/wakelock_profiler/active_max
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only longest active wakelocks, reported with name, duration in
		milliseconds, and rate. Writing "reset" clears the active-maximum
		statistics.
